## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* a path beyond the one, or any product, support, tooling, workflow, package or lock file in the commit; ANY removed line; an existing assertion loosened or an existing name lost; an added name not in the claimed 19; a skip, `.only`, environment gate, sleep or provider branch in an added row; **a named target mutant SURVIVING at the head** (N1, N2, N3, N4, N6, job-if, job-needs, job-coe, prod-env, dev-uses, dev-dupkey, dev-removed, N5: row P and the object rows must go red) **or an equivalent (eq-comment-in, eq-comment-above, eq-quote, eq-trailing, eq-blank) turning any NEW row red**; a new row green for the wrong reason (the premise or the right-reason message shows the checker refused something else, or a row that no checker mutant and no disk mutant can turn red and is not a declared control); a new write, removal, spawn, request, listener, port literal or check-then-use pair; a raw non-ASCII byte in an added line; a ticket key, card id or person name in an added line or the commit message; a secret; the head moved; a red check-run; **a CodeQL alert open on the head or the merge ref (either threshold), a missing analysis at the verdict, or a dismissed alert the gate did not make but the count shows**; a textual conflict in Check 8; **a B628 hunk inside `web-build` or the audit lines, or the head test file going red against B628's real `ci.yml`**. *Major:* a builder claim contradicted by measurement (the 19 new cases, the 16-of-19 figure, the survivors table, 2918 -> 2937); a sampled mutant killed by fewer rows than claimed; a repeat red; the `yaml` import resolving under one pool only; the legitimate-edit round trip (plant L1) leaving the design unable to accept a legitimate edit by updating `AUDIT_STEPS` as the PR's own comment says (print the rows); the web unit job's counts not +19 over main's push run. *Minor/Note:* the gate-own boundaries GB1 to GB4 surviving (the pin is "name plus run" on two steps and three job keys, by Tuesday's ruling); the 16-red-per-drift fan-out of rows sharing one premise; the tripwire rows' keys needing an update with `AUDIT_STEPS`; the `"echo skipped"` string; the 9 OLD text rows going red under three equivalent edits (pre-existing, not in this PR); an unverified (unsigned) commit; the builder's 50-run repeats cut to your 10; the optional runs cut; a count that differs from the builder's with no verdict consequence.
**VERDICT RULES.** GO needs Checks 1 to 9 clean and measured, both CodeQL thresholds met on a COMPLETE scan (4 of 4 analyses at `a90a8bd`, 0 open alerts on the head and merge refs), every check-run `completed` `success`, 0 findings above Note. **While any check-run of the head is pending (the drafting read had eight) the verdict is at most GO WITH FINDINGS and its text carries `(conditional: CI pending: <names>)`, never a bare GO.** GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note only. NO GO on any Blocker or Major: state the fix-shape in prose (a further ADDED commit is a new head and needs its own gate round; this is round 1 of 2, row G-cap at `model-routing.md:111`: a second NO GO on the same class goes to the product owner) and a ONE-line question for the product owner only if a ruling is needed. NOT GATED = the head moved or the PR is not open. A security-shaped finding is a STOP for tier 1.
**VERDICT LINES (one place, binding).** **First line of STATUS (placeholder at Step 0: `GATE VERDICT B636: PENDING`; verdict form, one line):** `GATE VERDICT B636: #213 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> @ a90a8bd (round 1 of 2 - delta <1 path, 1 commit, +123 -0; removed lines 0 y/n; product/workflow/package files 0 y/n; one added import y/n; non-ASCII 0 y/n> - names <web base -> head tests, files; lost n added n (19); audit-dev.test.ts 21 -> 40; duplicates 0 y/n> - checker mutants <CM-a..CM-g, RM-1..3 as claimed y/n; CM-h CM-i CM-j result; declared controls <names>> - disk <OLD survivors reproduced n of m; NEW red 16 of 19 under each of n mutants y/n; equivalents green on every new row y/n; old rows red under equivalents n (pre-existing); tripwire rows green at head y/n; plant L1 round trip <ok|rows>; boundaries GB1-GB4 <survive y/n>> - suites <head: web n passed n failed n skipped n, lint rc n, typecheck rc n; 10 repeats per pool red n; yaml resolves in both pools y/n> - CI <n completed success of n; pending <names|none>> - CodeQL <analyses n of 4 at the head; open alerts head n merge n; dismissed n> - B628 <branch exists y/n; hunks inside web-build n; head test vs its ci.yml red n of 40 or simulation red n of 40; merge-tree rc n> - merge <mergeable_state; merge-tree vs main rc n; tree equals GitHub's y/n; up-to-date rule y/n> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS (start and verdict), instrument and load, Checks 1-9 each with the FAIL clock and evidence path, findings `B636-n` (severity, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, fix-shape in prose, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY; "none" is valid), the removed-lines statement, the checker-mutant table (mutant x new row, ran, red rows by name, restore proof), the OLD census table and the NEW battery table (mutant x old rows red x new rows red x ran), the equivalents table, the legitimate-edit table (L1, L2), the B628 table, the surv